cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the D-index or this code, please cite the manuscript and this repository."
title: "dindex: a two-group log-ratio index for microbial community tables"
abstract: >-
  Python and R implementation of the D-index, D = (P - M)/(P + M) = tanh(0.5 ln(P/M)), a bounded
  two-group log-ratio index of microbial community composition, with quality-control flags,
  count-based and bootstrap intervals, and calibration helpers (environmental sensitivity, the
  value of the driver at which D = 0, and seasonal-baseline anomalies). This repository also
  contains the analysis and figure code for the accompanying manuscript on an
  Imitervirales-Algavirales balance in marine giant-virus communities.
